WEBVTT

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:34.900
<i>Episode 10</i>

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:34.900
<i>Fortress Beyond Compare</i>

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:40.240
The Tokugawa clan finally commenced 
their siege of Osaka Castle.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:43.380
Takatora Todo was entrusted with 
the attack from the south.

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:47.410
Sanada Maru

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:47.410
Standing in his way were Yukimura 
and the Sanada Maru.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:53.590
Lord Yukimura...

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:54.670
Not yet.

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:56.630
To the castle's east,

00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:01.680
Kanetsugu Naoe marched the Uesugi army 
toward the Yamato Bridge entrance.

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:03.930
Yamato Bridge

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.930
Keiji Maeda was tasked with its defense.

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:10.310
No one's getting past here.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:18.230
And to the west, the outer moat, and its many 
bridges, was the site of intense fighting

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:23.830
between Masamune Date's army and the 
forces led by Kiyomasa and Masanori.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:30.120
With gunners leading the way, the Date 
army looked to quickly break through.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:48.310
But the Toyotomi side held them off by destroying 
all the bridges across the moat.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:50.310
What now, losers?

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:53.310
Those two must be the enemy's defensive foundation.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:57.250
Ieyasu Tokugawa had set up camp at Mt. Chausu,

00:02:57.250 --> 00:03:00.320
southwest of Osaka Castle.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.320
Mt. Chausu

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:07.080
How do we overcome their geographical advantage?

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.990
We cannot wait any longer, Lord Yukimura.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:22.890
No, not yet.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:33.560
Open fire!

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:40.990
Don't let up!

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:45.570
Do not falter!

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.490
Cavalry, charge!

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.000
Gunners, take aim!

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:02.760
Fire!

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:23.030
On the first day of battle,

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:25.930
as the Tokugawa army looked to assert 
their numerical advantage,

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:30.790
the Toyotomi clan held them off with the moats 
that surrounded the castle on three sides.

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:34.270
Moreover, the Sanada Maru proved 
to be an impregnable wall,

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:36.470
successfully defending the southern side.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:41.050
I hear you fought well...

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:44.550
My men deserve all the credit 
for doing their jobs perfectly.

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:48.110
Thanks to you, troop morale is on the rise.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:50.740
They've taken to calling the 
Sanada Maru an unsinkable ship.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:53.810
After all, I'm its godfather.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:55.170
Oh.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.310
It's started to snow...

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.890
No wonder it's been so cold.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:02.820
Thanks, Tsukimaru.

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:08.820
"Sanada Maru"? What a ridiculous name.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:12.830
Today was merely the opening shot. 
There's no need to rush.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.580
The Toyotomi clan has nowhere to run.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:18.190
We can take our time and break them down.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:31.540
Yukimura seems to be the cornerstone 
of the Toyotomi clan's defense.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:34.860
He's an enemy of the Tokugawa clan.

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:36.850
We cannot leave him be.

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:50.390
Switch!

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:51.660
Hurry!

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:58.400
Why aren't we using our own gunners?

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:02.630
The enemy's firing from above, which means 
that they have longer range.

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:06.260
We need to get closer before we can return fire.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:08.380
Then hurry up and advance the troops!

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:11.890
The enemy seems to be having trouble 
switching their gunners.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:15.090
I'll take that chance to draw our men closer.

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:18.340
The enemy is gradually making up ground.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:21.900
Well, many of our men aren't familiar with guns.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.900
But I've already factored that into my plans.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:27.180
Lord Yukimura, does that mean...

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:27.950
Yes.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:29.540
Take charge.

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:30.350
Yes, sir.

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:35.480
Are we still not in range, Takatora?

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:36.790
We're almost there.

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:55.260
Wh-What?

00:06:59.110 --> 00:07:00.810
Wh-What's going on?

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:02.650
He had troops lying in wait?

00:07:24.590 --> 00:07:31.550
Sanada Maru

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:28.870
Reeling from Yukimura's ambush, 
the Tokugawa clan soldiers were

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:31.550
driven into a corner in front of the Sanada Maru.

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:33.220
Capitalizing on this opportunity,

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:37.720
a fierce onslaught was launched from the 
Sanada Maru on the enemy below.

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:45.800
The war continued, back and forth,

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:49.450
and before long, it was December.

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:55.780
Lord Hideyori,

00:07:56.220 --> 00:08:00.030
a month has passed since the war's start, 
and our men are tired from the fighting.

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:03.290
We must settle things as soon as possible.

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:05.580
The same goes for our opponents.

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:09.300
They're also in unfamiliar lands, 
which must be making it hard for them.

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:11.800
It's time we went on the offensive.

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:15.270
On every front, we're having 
trouble breaking through.

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:17.300
The outer moat, huh?

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:20.810
While that's definitely a factor, 
there's also the Sanada Maru.

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:24.130
It is crucial for us to bring that fortress down.

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:26.060
Yukimura Sanada...

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:33.070
Our men are starting to believe Osaka Castle 
can't be felled, with Yukimura at the helm.

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:35.630
This will hurt morale.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:38.830
Are you saying it'll be difficult to win this war?

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:41.040
Outer Enclosure 

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:42.670
Even if we manage to get past the Sanada Maru,

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:47.080
Main Keep

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:47.080
Second Line

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:47.080
Third Line

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:47.080
Outer Enclosure

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:46.860
there's still the inner moat, and the 
second and third lines of defense.

00:08:47.810 --> 00:08:51.090
Getting to the main keep will 
prove next to impossible.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:53.000
Just wait a bit.

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:54.900
I've made arrangements.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:03.320
The recent cold wave is starting 
to drain our men of energy.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:07.100
Some are even suffering because 
their wounds refuse to heal.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:10.010
They've all long surpassed their limits.

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:12.500
We have to do something.

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:43.140
Fire.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.540
Cannons?

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:04.150
The main keep!

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:10.880
From that distance?

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:13.120
Unbelievable.

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:16.050
How can they hit the main keep 
from all the way over there?

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:19.800
I never thought they'd bypass the Sanada Maru 
and directly attack the main keep.

00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:26.560
Lord Hideyori, you must evacuate!

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:29.560
I cannot run away all by myself!

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:44.910
The main keep's getting hit.

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:46.410
It can't be!

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:49.320
Where are you going?

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:50.650
To destroy the cannons.

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:51.730
You mustn't!

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:53.190
Let me go instead.

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:03.810
You have to stay here, Lord Yukimura!

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:06.930
Right now, you're the only one 
who can command our men.

00:11:08.570 --> 00:11:09.550
Very well.

00:11:09.920 --> 00:11:10.390
I'm off.

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:14.040
The enemy's attacking!

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:15.190
Hold them off!

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:28.080
Lord Maeda, the main keep...

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:30.660
Talk about rough.

00:11:30.930 --> 00:11:32.860
What do we do, Kiyomasa?

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:35.050
Focus on the enemy in front of you.

00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:36.420
Damn it all!

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:03.360
That's enough!

00:12:11.600 --> 00:12:12.570
She disappeared?

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:14.610
Where did she go?

00:12:14.610 --> 00:12:15.860
She's hurt.

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:17.170
Ignore her.

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:19.320
Regroup and keep firing.

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:20.130
Yes, sir.

00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:31.710
I'm not being any use to Lord Yukimura.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:39.650
Artillery fire from the Tokugawa clan's cannons, 
nicknamed the "Nation Destroyers,"

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:43.160
continued, day and night, for several days.

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:53.600
The relentless sound of cannon fire 
and the ensuing destruction

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:56.060
gradually took their toll on the 
Toyotomi soldiers' minds.

00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:00.370
I'm sorry, Lord Yukimura...

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:01.670
I...

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:03.380
Don't worry about it.

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:04.640
How are your wounds?

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:06.180
I'm fine.

00:13:06.540 --> 00:13:11.180
The Tokugawa clan sure had a 
hell of an ace up its sleeve.

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:14.680
Cease the artillery fire, you say?

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:17.690
It has already proven plenty effective.

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:21.480
If I may be so bold, at this rate, 
both sides will be destroyed.

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:23.690
What do you mean by "both sides"?

00:13:24.020 --> 00:13:25.970
The Toyotomi clan by the Nation Destroyers,

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:28.700
and us by the cold.

00:13:31.300 --> 00:13:34.940
This cold has our men 
growing weaker by the day.

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:38.210
We must not ignore it.

00:13:38.530 --> 00:13:41.210
Even so, we cannot stop now!

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:45.220
How about suggesting a truce, then?

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:47.190
Are you telling us to make peace?

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:49.260
I shall head to the castle as messenger.

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:49.840
Nonsense—

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:51.720
But I won't stop firing.

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:53.310
That's fine.

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:57.980
If they reject the truce, what will you do?

00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:01.230
Then I shall...

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:08.210
I shall let the men know.

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:09.620
No, I'm going alone.

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:11.240
Alone?

00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:14.370
Lord Ieyasu says he won't stop firing.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.180
I cannot endanger my men's lives.

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:19.900
I'd feel much more at ease alone.

00:14:19.900 --> 00:14:22.950
I admire your courage. Allow me to help.

00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:26.520
The castle is surrounded by rivers 
and moats on three sides.

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:28.260
It won't be easy to get past them.

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:32.510
Then the only way in is to the south, 
through the Sanada Maru?

00:14:34.460 --> 00:14:36.270
I will keep Yukimura occupied.

00:14:38.050 --> 00:14:39.270
You have my thanks.

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:42.790
No need. I was simply impressed by your resolve.

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:44.280
Let us be on our way.

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:45.150
Yes.

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:53.530
Does he want to wag his tail for 
the Tokugawa clan that badly?

00:14:54.050 --> 00:14:55.400
Lord Hidetada?

00:14:55.400 --> 00:14:56.290
What are you saying?

00:14:56.290 --> 00:15:00.040
I guess you'd expect as much from a man 
who'd let his brother die...

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:13.520
Please forgive my impudence!

00:15:40.010 --> 00:15:41.380
Follow my lead!

00:15:42.930 --> 00:15:44.250
Lord Kanetsugu?

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:52.470
Lord Kanetsugu!

00:15:52.870 --> 00:15:53.960
Yukimura...

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:11.220
Hurry up with the ammunition!

00:16:12.390 --> 00:16:13.490
Was that...

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:21.700
What's wrong?

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:23.360
Come at me!

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:31.260
Tadakatsu Honda, eh?

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:35.260
Keiji Maeda...

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:53.280
The preparations are complete, my lord.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.280
All right.

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:56.680
What are they trying to pull?

00:16:57.430 --> 00:16:58.240
Don't tell me...

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:16.900
They're using turrets as bridges!

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:18.400
Repel them!

00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:47.710
The castle's western defense hinges on you two.

00:17:48.740 --> 00:17:51.210
If we kill you, the west is ours.

00:17:51.520 --> 00:17:53.090
Keep talking, Masamune!

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:54.840
We'll turn the tables on you!

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:24.450
Masanori!

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:48.710
Lord Yukimura...

00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:50.010
Stay back!

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:51.760
Lord Nobuyuki's broken into the castle!

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:52.400
Huh?

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:55.150
He's gone to negotiate a truce.

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:56.900
What did you just say?!

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:09.900
That's Tadakatsu Honda for you.

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:12.710
I haven't had a fight this exciting in ages.

00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:14.210
Likewise.

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:17.470
Nice... Just how I like it.

00:19:17.470 --> 00:19:18.620
Lord Maeda!

00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:20.490
I'm busy!

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:22.650
Nobuyuki Sanada has broken into the main keep!

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:23.900
Huh?

00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:26.470
So that's your game.

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:36.040
Nobuyuki Sanada.

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:38.670
Lord Hideyori,

00:19:38.670 --> 00:19:40.990
I'm here as Lord Ieyasu's messenger.

00:19:44.630 --> 00:19:46.460
If this war continues,

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:50.170
both the Toyotomi and Tokugawa clans 
will be damaged beyond repair.

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:52.250
Please call a truce.

00:19:57.650 --> 00:19:58.750
Brother!

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:00.450
Stay out of this.

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:04.760
What will you do if Lord Hideyori rejects the truce?

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:06.980
You should already know the answer.

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:18.440
Stand down, Yukimura.

00:20:21.350 --> 00:20:24.780
Let the Tokugawa clan and us talk it out.

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:27.530
A wise decision.

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:31.000
Are you sure?

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:36.290
Look at the state we're in.

00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:48.380
If I don't stop this war, who will?

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:02.030
Nobuyuki did it, huh?

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:07.530
Cease fire.

00:21:27.630 --> 00:21:31.250
Kiyo... Kiyomasa...

00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:37.650
Kiyomasa!

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:57.480
The Tokugawa clan won't leave 
the Toyotomi standing.

00:22:01.640 --> 00:22:04.890
Next time will be to the death.

00:23:41.900 --> 00:23:45.150
Sengoku Musou 
High School

00:23:41.900 --> 00:23:45.150
10th Period

00:23:45.660 --> 00:23:47.480
This will be on the exam!

00:23:47.750 --> 00:23:50.880
"This will be on the exam"...

00:23:59.620 --> 00:24:01.920
Don't worry, Yukimura. I'm watching you.

00:24:02.560 --> 00:24:03.830
B-Brother?

00:24:03.830 --> 00:24:05.460
Not again, Nobuyuki!

00:24:05.460 --> 00:24:06.710
Get back to your class!

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:08.880
He's been seen!

00:24:08.880 --> 00:24:09.840
<i>To Be Continued</i>

00:24:09.840 --> 00:24:24.850
<i>Next Episode</i>

00:24:10.470 --> 00:24:13.930
The next decision is to willingly 
walk down a path of thorns.

00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:17.230
Does a bright future await beyond?

00:24:17.230 --> 00:24:18.600
Or is it the darkness of despair?

00:24:19.090 --> 00:24:22.150
The curtain now rises on the final battle.

00:24:22.150 --> 00:24:24.980
Next time: "The Lofty Castle."

00:24:22.850 --> 00:24:24.850
<i>Episode Eleven 
The Lofty Castle</i>
